er conditioning on being Sasha would change that, and it looks like it would only push toward inconsistent choices, so I'll go with the theory's answer and pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying P-FDT here, treating the two prisoner copies as running the same function on different inputs, with a policy that maps what each one sees to an action. The open question is which agent's years the unconditioned utility should count, and I'm working through how that changes when the agent doesn't know which prisoner she is.\n\nI'm working out the payoffs for each policy pair: mutual silence gives two years each, mutual sending gives four, and a mixed policy averages out to 2.5. Quiet-quiet comes out best under the unconditioned evaluation. I'm checking whether conditioning on being Sasha would change that, and it looks like it would only push toward inconsistent choices, so I'll go with the theory's answer and pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9511,"completion_tokens":827,"total_tokens":10338,"cost":0.054584,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.054584,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038044,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01654},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":432,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}